
  riscvsim › demo 5 · Loops
  Add 1 to 10 and watch the counter count down.

   1  # Add 1 + 2 + ... + 10. x1 counts down from 10 and
   2  # x2 collects the sum; bne repeats until x1 is 0.
   3  addi x1, x0, 10    # counter
   4  addi x2, x0, 0     # sum
   5  loop:
   6  add  x2, x2, x1    # sum = sum + counter
   7  addi x1, x1, -1    # counter = counter - 1
   8  bne  x1, x0, loop  # again until the counter is 0

  cycle 1
    IF addi x1, x0, 10  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    counter x1 = 0 · sum x2 = 0x7ffffffc
    › The first instruction, addi, is fetched from memory.

  cycle 2
    IF addi x2, x0, 0  ID addi x1, x0, 10  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    counter x1 = 0 · sum x2 = 0x7ffffffc
    › addi is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 3
    IF add x2, x2, x1  ID addi x2, x0, 0  EX addi x1, x0, 10  MEM ·  WB ·
    counter x1 = 0 · sum x2 = 0x7ffffffc
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 4
    IF addi x1,x1,-1  ID add x2,x2,x1  EX addi x2,x0,0  MEM addi x1,x0…  WB ·
    counter x1 = 0 · sum x2 = 0x7ffffffc
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 5
    IF bne x1,x0…  ID addi x1,x1…  EX add x2,x2…  MEM addi x2,x0…  WB addi x1…
    ✓ x1 = 10
    counter x1 = 10 · sum x2 = 0x7ffffffc
    › add needs x2 and x1 from addi, so it is forwarded from the EX/MEM latch
      and nobody waits.

  cycle 6
    IF ·  ID bne x1,x0…  EX addi x1,x1,-1  MEM add x2,x2,x1  WB addi x2,x0,0
    ✓ x2 = 0
    counter x1 = 10 · sum x2 = 0
    › addi finishes and writes x2 = 0.

  cycle 7
    IF ·  ID ·  EX bne x1, x0, loop  MEM addi x1, x1, -1  WB add x2, x2, x1
    ✓ x2 = 10
    counter x1 = 10 · sum x2 = 10
    › bne needs x1 from addi, so it is forwarded from the EX/MEM latch and
      nobody waits.

  cycle 8
    IF add x2, x2, x1  ID flushed  EX ·  MEM bne x1,x0,loop  WB addi x1,x1,-1
    ✓ x1 = 9
    counter x1 = 9 · sum x2 = 10
    › addi finishes and writes x1 = 9.

  cycle 9
    IF addi x1,x1,-1  ID add x2, x2, x1  EX flushed  MEM ·  WB bne x1,x0,loop
    counter x1 = 9 · sum x2 = 10
    › add is decoded and reads its source registers.

